    <item>
      <title>集合论</title>
      <link>/posts/set-theory/</link>
      <pubDate>Fri, 02 Sep 2022 12:43:41 +0800</pubDate>
      <guid>/posts/set-theory/</guid>
      <description><![CDATA[<h1 id="集合的概念" data-numberify>集合的概念<a class="anchor ms-1" href="#集合的概念"></a></h1>
<blockquote>
<ul>
<li>A <strong>set</strong> is a group of objects. (simplest way)</li>
<li>By a <strong>set</strong> we mean any collection M into a whole of definite disinct objects m (which we called <strong>elements</strong> of M) of our perception or thought. (Cantor&rsquo;s way)</li>
</ul>
</blockquote>
<p><strong>集合</strong>（set）是由 <u>指定范围</u>内的<u>满足给定条件的所有对象</u>聚集在一起构成的，指定范围内的每一个对象称为这个集合的<strong>元素</strong>（element）。</p>]]></description>
    </item>
    
